1
00:00:25,926 --> 00:00:28,160
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,303
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:51,450
♪ ♪

4
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:55,580
Hurry up. Smithsonian's
sick! Come on!

5
00:01:55,649 --> 00:01:57,493
He looked fine two
hours ago, Tommy.

6
00:01:57,517 --> 00:01:58,950
Well, he's sick.

7
00:01:59,019 --> 00:02:01,352
He didn't want his sugar.

8
00:02:05,259 --> 00:02:06,457
There, see?

9
00:02:06,526 --> 00:02:08,293
He looks fine to me.

10
00:02:10,197 --> 00:02:11,429
I'll show you.

11
00:02:11,498 --> 00:02:12,542
Be careful now.

12
00:02:12,566 --> 00:02:14,510
He pasted me a
good one last week.

13
00:02:14,534 --> 00:02:17,769
He won't hurt me.
He's my friend.

14
00:02:21,508 --> 00:02:26,444
See? He won't take
his sugar. He's sick.

15
00:02:26,513 --> 00:02:27,913
I'll be damned.

16
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:29,314
What the hell's going on here?

17
00:02:29,383 --> 00:02:31,283
Smithsonian's coming
down with something.

18
00:02:31,351 --> 00:02:32,717
So call the vet.

19
00:02:32,786 --> 00:02:36,154
Why aren't those
stalls cleared out?

20
00:02:36,223 --> 00:02:37,555
He was concerned
about the horse.

21
00:02:37,624 --> 00:02:39,369
I've got a ton of hay coming in,

22
00:02:39,393 --> 00:02:40,604
no place to put it.

23
00:02:40,628 --> 00:02:41,908
Now get to work.

24
00:02:46,634 --> 00:02:48,433
Yes, sir, Mr. Clint.

25
00:02:48,502 --> 00:02:50,580
If I were you, I'd
spend a little less time

26
00:02:50,604 --> 00:02:55,340
sticking up for him and a
little more time doing your job.

27
00:03:02,882 --> 00:03:05,917
Hyah! Come on! Hyah! Get it!

28
00:03:07,321 --> 00:03:08,853
Move!

29
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:14,540
Yah!

30
00:03:17,631 --> 00:03:18,897
Yah!

31
00:03:22,102 --> 00:03:23,768
Move it! Move!

32
00:03:23,837 --> 00:03:27,004
Mrs. Taylor, that
horse is all lathered up.

33
00:03:27,074 --> 00:03:29,441
He tried to throw me.
I'm teaching him a lesson.

34
00:03:31,411 --> 00:03:34,312
Tell her she can't
ride Henry J like that!

35
00:03:34,381 --> 00:03:36,348
Tell the boss's wife she can't?

36
00:03:36,416 --> 00:03:37,816
I don't think so, Tommy.

37
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:39,217
Hyah!

38
00:03:39,286 --> 00:03:42,721
She's hurting him!

39
00:03:42,789 --> 00:03:44,489
Stop! Stop!

40
00:03:50,564 --> 00:03:51,830
Let go of me!

41
00:03:51,899 --> 00:03:52,931
Are you sure you're okay?

42
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,611
What the hell kind
of stunt was that?!

43
00:03:54,635 --> 00:03:55,867
I could have broken my neck!

44
00:03:55,936 --> 00:03:58,169
Your neck's not hurt.

45
00:03:58,238 --> 00:03:59,670
You idiot.

46
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,439
You were hurting Henry J.

47
00:04:01,508 --> 00:04:03,408
Get this moron out of my sight

48
00:04:03,477 --> 00:04:05,043
and keep him there!

49
00:04:05,112 --> 00:04:06,545
Tommy, let's go.

50
00:04:06,613 --> 00:04:07,657
Now! Come on, Tommy.

51
00:04:07,681 --> 00:04:09,125
Let's go. Get out of here.

52
00:04:09,149 --> 00:04:10,615
I'm telling my
husband about this.

53
00:04:10,684 --> 00:04:12,484
So am I.

54
00:04:13,987 --> 00:04:15,787
Dad wants to sell this horse.

55
00:04:15,855 --> 00:04:17,022
He'll be mad as hell

56
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:19,291
when he hears you've
ridden him into the ground.

57
00:04:19,359 --> 00:04:21,960
Nobody's gonna buy a
horse that isn't schooled.

58
00:04:22,029 --> 00:04:25,730
Nobody's gonna buy
one that's foundered.

59
00:04:25,799 --> 00:04:28,766
You walk that horse
till he's bone-dry.

60
00:04:30,971 --> 00:04:32,970
She's the boss.

61
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:36,641
Sandra's a witch. You walk him.

62
00:04:36,709 --> 00:04:39,311
Oh, and I wouldn't go sucking up

63
00:04:39,379 --> 00:04:41,512
to her today, if I were you.

64
00:04:41,581 --> 00:04:44,182
She might smell
what's on your breath.

65
00:04:48,555 --> 00:04:50,788
Come in.

66
00:04:50,857 --> 00:04:53,791
Mr. Clint said you
want to see me?

67
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:58,063
Tommy, how did you
know Smithsonian was sick?

68
00:04:58,131 --> 00:05:01,199
Oh, 'cause I knew.

69
00:05:01,268 --> 00:05:04,970
Dr. Simpkin says
that he can't even play

70
00:05:05,038 --> 00:05:06,171
with his friends no more.

71
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:08,206
Well, just for a while.

72
00:05:08,274 --> 00:05:11,176
And that's because we don't
want them to get sick, too.

73
00:05:11,244 --> 00:05:13,377
And because you
were so observant,

74
00:05:13,446 --> 00:05:16,314
Dr. Simpkin doesn't
think they will.

75
00:05:16,382 --> 00:05:19,384
I don't know how you do it,

76
00:05:19,453 --> 00:05:20,997
but once again,
you just saved us

77
00:05:21,021 --> 00:05:23,099
a lot of money in vet bills.

78
00:05:23,123 --> 00:05:24,856
Thank you.

79
00:05:26,393 --> 00:05:27,393
Oh...

80
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:31,474
Oh, no!

81
00:05:31,498 --> 00:05:32,575
It's, it's all right.

82
00:05:32,599 --> 00:05:33,665
No! No!

83
00:05:33,734 --> 00:05:36,867
No! It's all right. No big deal.

84
00:05:36,937 --> 00:05:39,170
But it was so
pretty, and I broke it.

85
00:05:39,239 --> 00:05:41,506
A little glue and it'll
be as good as new.

86
00:05:41,575 --> 00:05:43,942
I have glue.

87
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:45,243
I'll fix it, okay?

88
00:05:45,312 --> 00:05:46,645
Okay.

89
00:05:49,883 --> 00:05:51,349
I'll fix it real good, Sandra.

90
00:05:51,418 --> 00:05:53,217
Hello.

91
00:05:53,286 --> 00:05:54,786
Sandra, it's Patricia.

92
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:58,055
I fell off Henry J. And
I was mad at myself.

93
00:05:58,124 --> 00:06:00,625
And embarrassed.

94
00:06:00,694 --> 00:06:03,495
But I-I shouldn't have
taken it out on the horse.

95
00:06:03,563 --> 00:06:04,996
Or you.

96
00:06:05,065 --> 00:06:06,231
It's all right.

97
00:06:06,299 --> 00:06:07,365
No, it isn't.

98
00:06:07,434 --> 00:06:10,801
Um... let me
apologize in person.

99
00:06:10,871 --> 00:06:12,037
Come to dinner tonight.

100
00:06:12,106 --> 00:06:14,272
Oh, I'd like to, really, um,

101
00:06:14,341 --> 00:06:16,341
but I'm gonna be working late.

102
00:06:16,410 --> 00:06:17,876
Something urgent's come up.

103
00:06:17,944 --> 00:06:19,577
In fact, I need to talk to Dad.

104
00:06:19,646 --> 00:06:23,281
Oh... He's, he's taking a nap.

105
00:06:23,349 --> 00:06:24,816
You want me to wake him?

106
00:06:24,885 --> 00:06:27,853
No, it'll wait.

107
00:06:27,921 --> 00:06:29,766
May I have a rain
check on dinner?

108
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:30,790
Sure.

109
00:06:30,824 --> 00:06:32,156
Anytime.

110
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:34,458
Bye.

111
00:06:49,509 --> 00:06:50,775
What are you doing?

112
00:06:50,844 --> 00:06:53,077
Fixing Sandra's horse.

113
00:06:53,146 --> 00:06:54,245
What happened to it?

114
00:06:54,314 --> 00:06:58,049
Aw... I broke it when
she was kissing me.

115
00:06:58,118 --> 00:07:00,785
The rest of us can't
hardly say boo to her,

116
00:07:00,854 --> 00:07:02,553
and you got her kissing you.

117
00:07:02,623 --> 00:07:05,122
Sandra and me are friends.

118
00:07:05,192 --> 00:07:07,492
You ought to be; you
practically grew up together.

119
00:07:09,696 --> 00:07:12,030
Did you finish
stacking that hay?

120
00:07:14,167 --> 00:07:15,167
I forgot.

121
00:07:15,202 --> 00:07:16,601
Mr. Clint's gonna be mad.

122
00:07:16,670 --> 00:07:19,170
Not if you go back out
there and finish it up.

123
00:07:20,607 --> 00:07:21,706
It's okay.

124
00:07:21,775 --> 00:07:24,475
It takes a while
for that glue to dry.

125
00:07:26,847 --> 00:07:28,279
Okay.

126
00:07:39,259 --> 00:07:42,560
Sandra? Fixed your horse.

127
00:08:10,824 --> 00:08:12,958
Hey, Tommy.

128
00:08:14,027 --> 00:08:15,694
Tommy?

129
00:08:15,762 --> 00:08:17,762
What's wrong?

130
00:08:32,079 --> 00:08:33,079
Nothing there.

131
00:08:33,113 --> 00:08:34,445
He's in here!

132
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:35,714
Don't hurt him.

133
00:08:35,782 --> 00:08:37,816
Stay back.

134
00:08:51,831 --> 00:08:54,499
You come along now.

135
00:08:54,568 --> 00:08:56,701
Don't give us any trouble.

136
00:08:56,770 --> 00:08:59,738
Come on. Stand up, son.

137
00:09:03,443 --> 00:09:04,723
Come on.

138
00:09:12,819 --> 00:09:14,385
Easy now.

139
00:09:14,454 --> 00:09:15,798
Put the cuffs on him.

140
00:09:16,823 --> 00:09:17,967
Take it easy, son.

141
00:09:23,096 --> 00:09:24,240
Let me go, please! Stop it!

142
00:09:24,264 --> 00:09:26,142
Tommy! Let me go!
Let me go! Let me go!

143
00:09:26,166 --> 00:09:27,432
No!

144
00:09:27,501 --> 00:09:28,766
Tommy, stop it!

145
00:09:28,835 --> 00:09:31,436
Now stop fighting right now.

146
00:09:33,373 --> 00:09:37,342
Now Tommy, you do what the
policemen tell you to do, hear?

147
00:09:37,411 --> 00:09:39,643
Yes, sir.

148
00:09:39,712 --> 00:09:41,190
Put your hands behind your back.

149
00:10:28,061 --> 00:10:28,993
Hello, Sam.

150
00:10:29,062 --> 00:10:32,563
Ben.

151
00:10:32,633 --> 00:10:36,701
I, um, I read the paper.

152
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:38,970
I'm really sorry about Sandra.

153
00:10:39,039 --> 00:10:41,005
Thanks.

154
00:10:41,074 --> 00:10:43,341
Things sure are never
gonna be the same

155
00:10:43,410 --> 00:10:44,842
around here without her.

156
00:10:46,579 --> 00:10:49,580
Well, it's... it's been a
while. How you been?

157
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:51,516
Oh, fine, fine.

158
00:10:51,584 --> 00:10:56,287
The years have generally
treated me pretty good.

159
00:10:56,356 --> 00:10:59,490
Uh, Sam, uh...

160
00:10:59,559 --> 00:11:02,393
is there anything
I can do for you?

161
00:11:02,462 --> 00:11:06,030
There's nothing, really, Ben.

162
00:11:06,099 --> 00:11:07,598
Well, yeah, yeah.

163
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:10,168
The police have
arrested Tommy Jenks.

164
00:11:10,236 --> 00:11:11,802
Yeah, I read about that.

165
00:11:11,871 --> 00:11:13,137
Tommy's retarded.

166
00:11:13,206 --> 00:11:16,040
His father was one
of my best friends,

167
00:11:16,109 --> 00:11:17,741
and his mother
ran away from home

168
00:11:17,810 --> 00:11:19,711
when Tommy was
just five years old,

169
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:21,958
and then his father died
a few years after that.

170
00:11:21,982 --> 00:11:24,149
I raised him
alongside of Sandra.

171
00:11:24,217 --> 00:11:25,650
He's a good boy.

172
00:11:25,718 --> 00:11:28,552
Ben, he doesn't lie, and
he said he didn't do it.

173
00:11:28,621 --> 00:11:30,922
Oh, honey, I've been
looking all over for you.

174
00:11:30,991 --> 00:11:33,224
You should be up
at the house resting.

175
00:11:33,293 --> 00:11:35,059
I can't.

176
00:11:35,128 --> 00:11:36,527
I just lay there thinking.

177
00:11:36,596 --> 00:11:39,464
Oh, Ben, this is
my wife, Patricia.

178
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:42,800
Patricia, Ben Matlock,
a very old friend.

179
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:44,080
Hello. Hello.

180
00:11:44,104 --> 00:11:46,003
Honey, please.

181
00:11:46,073 --> 00:11:48,633
Tommy Jenks
wouldn't kill anybody.

182
00:11:48,675 --> 00:11:50,875
Bad enough losing Sandra, but...

183
00:11:52,578 --> 00:11:55,146
having Tommy accused of it...

184
00:11:55,215 --> 00:11:56,258
Can you help, Ben?

185
00:11:56,282 --> 00:11:58,842
It would, it would
mean the world to me.

186
00:12:00,787 --> 00:12:04,956
I knew Miss Sandra was dead,
'cause sometimes, on the farm,

187
00:12:05,025 --> 00:12:07,391
horses, they get dead.

188
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:09,572
They get all cold,
and they don't move,

189
00:12:09,596 --> 00:12:11,473
and that's just the way she was,

190
00:12:11,497 --> 00:12:14,933
and it made me scared to
see Miss Sandra like that.

191
00:12:17,170 --> 00:12:19,104
Come sit down.

192
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:29,313
That's why you ran away and hid?

193
00:12:33,252 --> 00:12:34,518
Can I go home now?

194
00:12:36,623 --> 00:12:37,755
No.

195
00:12:37,824 --> 00:12:39,156
Not, not yet.

196
00:12:39,225 --> 00:12:40,524
Oh.

197
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:43,027
I forgot to feed the horses
their oats this morning.

198
00:12:43,096 --> 00:12:44,395
Mr. Clint's gonna be so mad.

199
00:12:44,463 --> 00:12:45,575
Oh, I, oh, I'm sure

200
00:12:45,599 --> 00:12:47,932
Mr. Clint got somebody
else to do that.

201
00:12:48,001 --> 00:12:48,933
I hope so.

202
00:12:49,002 --> 00:12:50,167
I hope, I hope he did.

203
00:12:50,236 --> 00:12:52,336
Tommy, listen.

204
00:12:52,405 --> 00:12:53,504
Tommy, listen to me.

205
00:12:53,573 --> 00:12:56,074
Are... Are you listening?

206
00:12:56,143 --> 00:12:57,875
Yeah.

207
00:12:57,944 --> 00:12:59,224
Okay.

208
00:13:00,981 --> 00:13:04,882
Now, this may be hard
for you to understand,

209
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:08,152
but you have to try, okay?

210
00:13:08,221 --> 00:13:09,153
Okay.

211
00:13:09,222 --> 00:13:12,290
Okay.

212
00:13:12,359 --> 00:13:16,194
Some people think
you killed Sandra,

213
00:13:16,262 --> 00:13:19,897
and that means there's
going to have to be a trial.

214
00:13:19,966 --> 00:13:21,143
Are you with me?

215
00:13:21,167 --> 00:13:23,334
Do you understand?

216
00:13:23,403 --> 00:13:27,038
I didn't, I didn't clean
out the stalls either.

217
00:13:27,106 --> 00:13:30,041
Tommy, Tommy,
listen to me, listen to me.

218
00:13:32,312 --> 00:13:34,312
We can tell the judge...

219
00:13:34,381 --> 00:13:37,048
He's the man in
charge of the trial...

220
00:13:39,119 --> 00:13:42,586
that you wish to plead
diminished capacity.

221
00:13:42,656 --> 00:13:47,403
That means that
maybe you killed Sandra,

222
00:13:47,427 --> 00:13:50,194
but you didn't know
what you were doing

223
00:13:50,263 --> 00:13:51,795
and you didn't mean to.

224
00:13:51,865 --> 00:13:54,498
That's wrong!

225
00:13:54,567 --> 00:13:56,701
I didn't kill Sandra.

226
00:13:56,769 --> 00:13:58,548
But, Tommy, see, sometimes,

227
00:13:58,572 --> 00:14:04,042
- sometimes we have...
- Oh, Lord.

228
00:14:07,147 --> 00:14:13,451
Tommy... sometimes
we have to make a deal.

229
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:17,555
We tell the judge you did it,

230
00:14:17,623 --> 00:14:20,758
and in return,

231
00:14:20,826 --> 00:14:23,861
he sends you to a
hospital for awhile

232
00:14:23,930 --> 00:14:27,799
instead of to prison.

233
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:30,902
I don't, I don't want
to go to a hospital.

234
00:14:32,972 --> 00:14:34,705
I don't want to go to a prison.

235
00:14:36,776 --> 00:14:38,643
I want to go home.

236
00:14:38,712 --> 00:14:43,347
Tommy... I want to go home.

237
00:14:46,152 --> 00:14:47,585
Did you kill Sandra?

238
00:14:51,057 --> 00:14:53,858
Tommy would never hurt Sandra.

239
00:14:56,963 --> 00:15:01,165
Then that's what we'll have
to prove to a judge and jury.

240
00:15:01,233 --> 00:15:02,233
Okay?

241
00:15:03,269 --> 00:15:05,937
Okay.

242
00:15:06,005 --> 00:15:07,504
Can I go home now?

243
00:15:07,574 --> 00:15:12,310
Tommy... I'm gonna try.

244
00:15:23,390 --> 00:15:26,190
Your Honor, the State feels

245
00:15:26,259 --> 00:15:29,594
a complete psychiatric
examination of the defendant

246
00:15:29,663 --> 00:15:32,964
is necessary in order to
determine whether he is

247
00:15:33,033 --> 00:15:34,532
competent to stand trial.

248
00:15:34,601 --> 00:15:36,300
We have reason to believe

249
00:15:36,369 --> 00:15:39,536
Mr. Jenks lacks
sufficient capacity

250
00:15:39,606 --> 00:15:41,705
to know, understand
and appreciate

251
00:15:41,774 --> 00:15:43,707
the charges against him.

252
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:45,042
However, I'm sure

253
00:15:45,111 --> 00:15:46,644
defense counsel
and I can agree...

254
00:15:46,713 --> 00:15:48,378
Uh, uh, Y-Your Honor...

255
00:15:48,447 --> 00:15:51,015
Uh, excuse me for
interrupting, Ms. March,

256
00:15:51,084 --> 00:15:53,229
but I believe I can
save us all a lot of time.

257
00:15:53,253 --> 00:15:57,888
Uh, a complete psychiatric
exam and evaluation,

258
00:15:57,957 --> 00:16:01,292
uh, on my client, has
just been completed

259
00:16:01,361 --> 00:16:04,361
by Dr. Samuel Chadwick.

260
00:16:04,430 --> 00:16:07,031
Uh, I believe you
know Dr. Chadwick.

261
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:09,834
He's provided you with expert
testimony on several occasions.

262
00:16:09,903 --> 00:16:11,047
Yes, I know Dr. Chadwick...

263
00:16:11,071 --> 00:16:12,736
Well, as it happens,

264
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:15,373
Dr. Chadwick
knows my client, too.

265
00:16:15,442 --> 00:16:17,041
Has for many years.

266
00:16:17,110 --> 00:16:19,643
And after reacquainting himself

267
00:16:19,713 --> 00:16:22,546
with my client,
uh, in an interview,

268
00:16:22,615 --> 00:16:25,027
he prepared this evaluation.

269
00:16:25,051 --> 00:16:27,618
In it, he concludes that

