00:16:27,687 --> 00:16:30,654
"Tommy Jenks is
a benign individual

271
00:16:30,723 --> 00:16:33,992
"who possesses great
respect for authority figures,

272
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:37,161
"is emotionally
attached to his home

273
00:16:37,230 --> 00:16:39,464
"out at the Taylor
thoroughbred farm,

274
00:16:39,532 --> 00:16:43,600
and that he is unequivocally
competent to stand trial."

275
00:16:45,672 --> 00:16:47,505
Do you know what you're doing?

276
00:16:47,574 --> 00:16:51,175
You just blew the opportunity
to plead diminished capacity

277
00:16:51,244 --> 00:16:52,276
and/or insanity.

278
00:16:52,345 --> 00:16:53,611
I know.

279
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:55,524
I see no reason why the court

280
00:16:55,548 --> 00:16:57,259
shouldn't accept
this evaluation.

281
00:16:57,283 --> 00:16:59,851
Ms. March?

282
00:16:59,919 --> 00:17:02,220
I... I suppose I see
no objection either.

283
00:17:02,288 --> 00:17:03,520
Oh, good.

284
00:17:03,589 --> 00:17:07,058
Your Honor, uh, defense
waives reading of the charges,

285
00:17:07,127 --> 00:17:09,560
pleads innocent and
wishes to proceed

286
00:17:09,629 --> 00:17:11,340
directly to the matter of bail.

287
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:13,897
Ms. March, any recommendations?

288
00:17:13,967 --> 00:17:15,299
Yes.

289
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:16,534
Yes, Your Honor.

290
00:17:16,603 --> 00:17:21,171
Um, in view of the
fact that the defendant

291
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:23,608
stands accused
of a capital crime

292
00:17:23,676 --> 00:17:26,711
and has tried to escape
justice by resisting arrest,

293
00:17:26,780 --> 00:17:30,180
the State asks that bail be
set at one hun... $250,000.

294
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:32,061
Uh, Your Honor...

295
00:17:32,085 --> 00:17:34,752
I'd like to remind
the prosecutor

296
00:17:34,821 --> 00:17:38,789
that she has agreed with
Dr. Chadwick's conclusion

297
00:17:38,858 --> 00:17:41,559
that Tommy Jenks is
a harmless individual,

298
00:17:41,627 --> 00:17:42,705
does what he's told

299
00:17:42,729 --> 00:17:45,563
and has strong ties
to his community.

300
00:17:45,632 --> 00:17:48,032
Bail is $25,000.

301
00:17:48,101 --> 00:17:50,546
Trial is set for April 16.

302
00:17:51,838 --> 00:17:54,071
Can I go home now?

303
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:55,306
Yeah.

304
00:17:55,375 --> 00:17:57,908
Come on, Tommy.

305
00:17:57,977 --> 00:17:58,977
I'm going home.

306
00:18:14,661 --> 00:18:17,461
Well, Sam said he'd be

307
00:18:17,530 --> 00:18:19,429
up this road, just
past the house.

308
00:18:19,498 --> 00:18:20,575
Want me to drive you?

309
00:18:20,599 --> 00:18:21,532
No, that's okay.

310
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,534
The walk will do me good.

311
00:18:57,603 --> 00:18:59,637
Sam, when you take a walk,

312
00:18:59,706 --> 00:19:02,151
you just go ahead and
take one, don't you?

313
00:19:02,175 --> 00:19:03,974
Two miles out, two miles back.

314
00:19:04,043 --> 00:19:06,188
That's supposed to keep me
from getting another heart attack.

315
00:19:06,212 --> 00:19:08,712
Oh, yeah, yeah.

316
00:19:08,781 --> 00:19:10,548
What's, uh, what's in there?

317
00:19:10,617 --> 00:19:13,117
It's a grave.

318
00:19:13,185 --> 00:19:15,820
Best horse I ever
had's buried there.

319
00:19:15,888 --> 00:19:16,821
Knight's Legend.

320
00:19:16,889 --> 00:19:18,689
You remember?

321
00:19:18,757 --> 00:19:19,801
Oh, that's right.

322
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:21,236
He won the Triple Crown.

323
00:19:21,260 --> 00:19:22,304
Yeah.

324
00:19:22,328 --> 00:19:24,228
Broke his leg winning
the Peach Tree Stakes

325
00:19:24,297 --> 00:19:25,396
about four years ago.

326
00:19:25,465 --> 00:19:28,232
I had to put him down.

327
00:19:28,301 --> 00:19:30,667
I had my heart attack
just a few days after that.

328
00:19:30,737 --> 00:19:32,769
Couldn't you have
patched him up?

329
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:34,871
Well, maybe; maybe not.

330
00:19:34,940 --> 00:19:38,275
But he was in such pain...

331
00:19:38,344 --> 00:19:39,876
Sandra said I was wrong.

332
00:19:39,945 --> 00:19:41,490
She said I...

333
00:19:41,514 --> 00:19:44,548
that I lost a ton of
money in stud fees.

334
00:19:44,617 --> 00:19:48,018
But I just couldn't
see him going like that.

335
00:19:48,087 --> 00:19:52,356
Sandra always did say
I was no businessman.

336
00:19:52,425 --> 00:19:53,536
That...

337
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:55,200
that's why she took
over running the farm.

338
00:19:55,227 --> 00:19:57,628
Thank God she did.

339
00:19:57,697 --> 00:20:00,698
I was borrowing
money right and left.

340
00:20:00,767 --> 00:20:03,367
How she kept us out of
bankruptcy, I'll never know.

341
00:20:03,436 --> 00:20:06,470
Uh, how long, how long
you been married to Patricia?

342
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:09,373
Oh, about two years.

343
00:20:09,442 --> 00:20:11,153
Things were starting
to pick up then.

344
00:20:11,177 --> 00:20:12,109
Uh-huh.

345
00:20:12,178 --> 00:20:13,577
I guess, uh,

346
00:20:13,646 --> 00:20:17,014
Sandra and Patricia got
along pretty well, didn't they?

347
00:20:18,618 --> 00:20:21,551
Patricia was only five
years older than Sandra.

348
00:20:21,621 --> 00:20:23,587
That didn't make
it easy for Sandra.

349
00:20:24,958 --> 00:20:29,259
And Sandra insisted that Pat
sign a prenuptial agreement.

350
00:20:29,328 --> 00:20:30,406
Oh, well...

351
00:20:30,430 --> 00:20:32,140
That didn't make
it easy for Pat.

352
00:20:32,164 --> 00:20:34,064
That's good though.

353
00:20:34,133 --> 00:20:36,567
You know...

354
00:20:36,636 --> 00:20:39,369
women are a lot more
complicated than horses.

355
00:20:40,907 --> 00:20:42,083
Yeah.

356
00:20:42,107 --> 00:20:43,387
Yeah, you're right.

357
00:20:51,183 --> 00:20:54,118
Okay.

358
00:21:12,639 --> 00:21:15,139
Oh, she's a beauty.

359
00:21:15,207 --> 00:21:16,874
Hi again.

360
00:21:16,943 --> 00:21:17,975
Michelle Thomas.

361
00:21:18,044 --> 00:21:19,454
We met at Tommy's hearing.

362
00:21:19,478 --> 00:21:20,478
Right. Hello.

363
00:21:20,513 --> 00:21:21,445
Hi.

364
00:21:21,514 --> 00:21:22,557
Brood mare. Just bought her.

365
00:21:22,581 --> 00:21:23,792
Actually, practically stole her.

366
00:21:23,816 --> 00:21:24,816
Come on.

367
00:21:24,884 --> 00:21:26,684
Turn her loose in the
paddock for a walk.

368
00:21:26,753 --> 00:21:27,852
Yes, ma'am.

369
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:29,364
Well, it looks like
you've pretty much

370
00:21:29,388 --> 00:21:31,700
taken charge of
things around here.

371
00:21:31,724 --> 00:21:32,923
Somebody had to.

372
00:21:32,992 --> 00:21:36,993
Since Sam's heart attack,
he can't do too much.

373
00:21:37,062 --> 00:21:40,197
Uh, if you'll excuse me,
I'd like to go clean up.

374
00:21:40,265 --> 00:21:44,034
Um, were you home the
night Sandra was murdered?

375
00:21:44,102 --> 00:21:45,469
Yes.

376
00:21:45,538 --> 00:21:49,340
Did you see or hear
anything out of the ordinary?

377
00:21:49,408 --> 00:21:51,107
Nope.

378
00:21:51,176 --> 00:21:54,110
What about your husband?

379
00:21:54,179 --> 00:21:57,981
Actually, Sam went into town
for about an hour after dinner.

380
00:21:58,050 --> 00:22:01,051
And, uh, when he came
back, that's when I told him

381
00:22:01,119 --> 00:22:03,787
Sandra had mentioned that
she wanted to talk to him.

382
00:22:03,856 --> 00:22:05,288
That's when he found the body.

383
00:22:05,358 --> 00:22:08,959
Well, what made you think
she'd still be in her office?

384
00:22:09,028 --> 00:22:12,363
She told me she'd
be working late.

385
00:22:12,432 --> 00:22:15,065
When I called to apologize for
something that happened earlier.

386
00:22:15,134 --> 00:22:18,101
Oh, you had an argument?

387
00:22:18,171 --> 00:22:21,137
Ms. Thomas, make up your mind

388
00:22:21,206 --> 00:22:24,108
whether you and Mr. Matlock
are defending Tommy

389
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:26,810
or prosecuting me.

390
00:22:26,879 --> 00:22:28,279
Excuse me.

391
00:22:35,888 --> 00:22:39,690
Donovan, haul a bale of hay
out to the paddock and break it up.

392
00:22:39,758 --> 00:22:40,958
New mare's out there.

393
00:22:41,027 --> 00:22:42,926
I'll do it, Mr. Clint!

394
00:22:42,995 --> 00:22:44,628
I said Donovan.

395
00:22:44,697 --> 00:22:48,832
After all, you're not gonna
be around here much longer.

396
00:22:48,901 --> 00:22:50,367
Well, I'm not going anyplace.

397
00:22:50,436 --> 00:22:52,836
Hell, you're going to prison.

398
00:22:52,905 --> 00:22:53,837
Cut it out, Clint.

399
00:22:53,906 --> 00:22:56,473
It's a scary place, kid.

400
00:22:56,542 --> 00:23:01,011
Well, Mr. Matlock, he
said I was gonna stay here.

401
00:23:01,079 --> 00:23:02,312
He lied.

402
00:23:02,382 --> 00:23:04,727
They're gonna put you away, boy.

403
00:23:04,751 --> 00:23:06,684
No!

404
00:23:12,491 --> 00:23:14,691
What the hell'd you do that for?

405
00:23:22,401 --> 00:23:26,848
Well... I'll bet you
didn't have to do

406
00:23:26,872 --> 00:23:29,084
much of that when
you were foreman.

407
00:23:29,108 --> 00:23:30,040
Ben Matlock.

408
00:23:30,109 --> 00:23:31,742
Yes, sir.

409
00:23:34,847 --> 00:23:38,115
Must have been quite
a shock when she...

410
00:23:38,184 --> 00:23:40,817
chose Clint and
demoted you that way.

411
00:23:40,887 --> 00:23:42,452
Didn't make me real happy.

412
00:23:42,522 --> 00:23:45,989
Must not have made you too mad.

413
00:23:46,058 --> 00:23:47,491
You're still here.

414
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:49,092
I'm ten years
past starting over.

415
00:23:49,162 --> 00:23:50,661
Sandra knew that.

416
00:23:50,729 --> 00:23:53,597
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

417
00:23:53,666 --> 00:23:57,000
Um, anything else you
want to know, Mr. Matlock?

418
00:23:57,069 --> 00:23:59,970
Well, yeah.

419
00:24:00,039 --> 00:24:03,340
You got any idea
who killed Sandra?

420
00:24:03,408 --> 00:24:04,875
No.

421
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:08,812
You think it was Tommy?

422
00:24:10,816 --> 00:24:13,750
I can't believe it was Tommy.

423
00:24:13,819 --> 00:24:14,819
It wasn't me.

424
00:24:14,887 --> 00:24:16,327
I was in the bunkhouse reading

425
00:24:16,355 --> 00:24:18,288
right up till the time
the police came.

426
00:24:18,357 --> 00:24:21,324
Uh, you couldn't have maybe gone

427
00:24:21,394 --> 00:24:22,738
you know, somewhere...?

428
00:24:22,762 --> 00:24:25,061
What the Sam Hill?!

429
00:24:25,130 --> 00:24:26,963
Somebody's starting my truck!

430
00:24:27,032 --> 00:24:29,800
That's Tommy!

431
00:24:36,175 --> 00:24:40,443
Tommy! Tommy, come back here!

432
00:24:44,383 --> 00:24:46,943
What the hell got into him?

433
00:25:40,940 --> 00:25:42,606
♪ ♪

434
00:25:45,511 --> 00:25:46,876
Here you go.

435
00:25:46,945 --> 00:25:49,146
Ice machine's behind the office

436
00:25:49,215 --> 00:25:50,447
next to the pop machine.

437
00:25:50,516 --> 00:25:52,516
And don't go
smacking the TV around

438
00:25:52,585 --> 00:25:54,028
thinking it's broken,
'cause it ain't.

439
00:25:54,052 --> 00:25:56,186
Cable's out, so it only
gets two channels.

440
00:25:56,255 --> 00:25:58,288
That'll be 18 bucks.

441
00:26:09,502 --> 00:26:12,202
Need anything else,
just give me a holler

442
00:26:25,150 --> 00:26:27,717
We don't have the
money to do that right now

443
00:26:27,786 --> 00:26:29,853
and you know it! The
business isn't going that well!

444
00:26:29,921 --> 00:26:31,366
I'm not talking about money!

445
00:26:31,390 --> 00:26:33,001
I'm talking about
what you promised!

446
00:26:33,025 --> 00:26:36,026
I don't even
remember! You're crazy!

447
00:26:36,095 --> 00:26:39,997
I can't... What am
I...? I can't trust you!

448
00:26:40,065 --> 00:26:41,631
Give me that
briefcase! Gimme it!

449
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:42,999
No, no!

450
00:26:43,069 --> 00:26:44,712
Give it here! What's in here?!

451
00:26:44,736 --> 00:26:46,870
I'll punch ya!

452
00:26:46,939 --> 00:26:48,383
Ah...

453
00:26:48,407 --> 00:26:53,777
Congratulations, Sydney, I hear
you're kicking the banana habit.

454
00:26:53,846 --> 00:26:55,979
Oh, I am, Stanley, I am, I am!

455
00:26:58,283 --> 00:27:00,718
As soon as my
emergency supply is gone.

456
00:27:05,224 --> 00:27:08,291
Oh, I feel so
refreshed. So refreshed.

457
00:27:15,067 --> 00:27:16,400
Hi, Sidney.

458
00:27:17,737 --> 00:27:19,936
Ah! For heaven's sakes,
Cleo, you startled me.

459
00:27:20,005 --> 00:27:22,951
I'm gonna call the manager
if you don't turn that TV down!

460
00:27:24,142 --> 00:27:26,054
I'm sorry, Sidney. We
just want you to know

461
00:27:26,078 --> 00:27:28,211
that we're proud of
what you're doing.

462
00:27:28,280 --> 00:27:30,781
And we're going to help
you fight the banana habit.

463
00:27:32,718 --> 00:27:34,362
Who needs help? Who needs it?

464
00:27:34,386 --> 00:27:36,286
You will, Sydney,

465
00:27:36,355 --> 00:27:40,991
when the wind comes
from the banana plantation.

466
00:27:41,059 --> 00:27:42,259
I'll punch you!

467
00:27:42,294 --> 00:27:45,262
Oh, no, the wind has
shifted toward the jungle!

468
00:27:45,330 --> 00:27:46,410
That crazy elephant...

469
00:27:47,900 --> 00:27:51,235
Uh, hey, Mr. Donovan.

470
00:27:52,605 --> 00:27:55,838
You got a minute? I want
to ask you something.

471
00:28:41,954 --> 00:28:44,754
Mr. Purdy... What do you want?

472
00:28:44,823 --> 00:28:46,568
Did you run Tommy off on purpose

473
00:28:46,592 --> 00:28:48,270
or was it just
regular stupidity?

474
00:28:48,294 --> 00:28:50,138
I figured it was time
somebody leveled with him.

475
00:28:50,162 --> 00:28:52,629
That was a jackass thing to do

476
00:28:52,698 --> 00:28:54,031
and you know it.

477
00:28:54,100 --> 00:28:57,901
Where were you when
Sandra Taylor was killed?

478
00:28:57,970 --> 00:29:01,037
I don't remember.

479
00:29:01,106 --> 00:29:03,574
Me and Sandra
got along just fine,

480
00:29:03,642 --> 00:29:05,641
and that's all I got to say.

481
00:29:16,589 --> 00:29:18,388
Hmm.

482
00:29:37,143 --> 00:29:38,508
And the farmer eats it.

483
00:29:38,577 --> 00:29:41,678
Great pig like that, you
don't eat 'em all at once.

484
00:29:48,053 --> 00:29:49,333
Hey...

485
00:29:49,388 --> 00:29:53,157
Hey, you play one mean
game of video there, boy.

486
00:29:53,225 --> 00:29:54,724
Thank you.

487
00:29:54,794 --> 00:29:56,126
It's real easy.

488
00:29:56,195 --> 00:29:58,395
You just shoot these
little guys with this.

489
00:29:58,463 --> 00:30:00,997
Lyle, Lyle, now,
did you hear that?

490
00:30:01,066 --> 00:30:04,100
Why, I bet we... I bet we got us

491
00:30:04,169 --> 00:30:05,769
a college graduate
here or something.

492
00:30:05,838 --> 00:30:08,972
Yeah, maybe a rocket scientist.

493
00:30:09,041 --> 00:30:12,643
You a rocket
scientist, boy, hmm?

494
00:30:14,212 --> 00:30:16,725
Oh, hey, where you going?

495
00:30:16,749 --> 00:30:18,948
You guys are teasing me.

496
00:30:19,017 --> 00:30:20,017
No, we're not.

497
00:30:20,051 --> 00:30:23,086
Yes, you are.

498
00:30:23,155 --> 00:30:24,599
Oh, did you hear that, Jed? Huh?

499
00:30:24,623 --> 00:30:26,268
I think he just
called me a liar.

500
00:30:26,292 --> 00:30:29,025
Now... now, you
gotta understand...

501
00:30:29,094 --> 00:30:30,360
Lyle here's my friend.

502
00:30:30,429 --> 00:30:33,430
And I don't like it when
people call him a liar.

503
00:30:33,499 --> 00:30:35,365
I don't like it at all.

504
00:30:35,434 --> 00:30:37,367
Whoa! You captured him!

505
00:30:37,436 --> 00:30:39,803
Good work, gentlemen.

506
00:30:39,872 --> 00:30:44,374
Now speak very softly
and watch what you say.

507
00:30:44,443 --> 00:30:47,777
And who are you?

508
00:30:47,847 --> 00:30:51,315
I am Dr. Tyler Hudson,
criminal psychiatrist.

509
00:30:51,383 --> 00:30:56,720
And you gentlemen have just
captured a very dangerous man.

510
00:30:56,789 --> 00:30:58,499
Come on.

511
00:30:58,523 --> 00:30:59,956
This half-wit?

512
00:31:00,025 --> 00:31:04,928
Hey, watch what you say
or you may set him off again.

513
00:31:04,997 --> 00:31:06,929
What do you mean, set him off?

514
00:31:06,999 --> 00:31:09,933
Let's put it this way:

515
00:31:10,002 --> 00:31:11,746
there were three
of us escorting him

516
00:31:11,770 --> 00:31:13,770
to a violent ward.

517
00:31:13,839 --> 00:31:21,839
Somebody said the wrong
thing. I'm the only one still walking.

518
00:31:23,081 --> 00:31:28,084
Tommy, Mr. Matlock
sent me for you.

519
00:31:28,153 --> 00:31:30,887
Come with me, okay?

520
00:31:40,065 --> 00:31:41,497
Is he mad?

521
00:31:41,566 --> 00:31:44,134
Naw, he's not mad.

522
00:31:44,203 --> 00:31:46,836
He knows you didn't mean
to break Dr. Scribner's neck.

523
00:31:49,041 --> 00:31:51,408
Come on.

524
00:32:07,459 --> 00:32:08,391
Okay.

525
00:32:08,460 --> 00:32:12,762
1-65-83-24. You got it, Ben.

526
00:32:12,831 --> 00:32:15,632
Thank you.

527
00:32:15,700 --> 00:32:18,335
Well, Sandra's
leather briefcase.

528
00:32:18,403 --> 00:32:20,270
Here's a telephone book.

529
00:32:20,339 --> 00:32:23,259
Okay... Maybe we'll
find something in here.

530
00:32:25,877 --> 00:32:27,710
These are old calendars.

531
00:32:27,780 --> 00:32:29,780
Huh, that's odd.

532
00:32:29,848 --> 00:32:33,250
Well, maybe she was
cleaning out her files.

533
00:32:33,318 --> 00:32:35,263
Why would she put
these old calendars,

534
00:32:35,287 --> 00:32:37,753
all this wrinkled
stuff in her briefcase?

535
00:32:37,823 --> 00:32:39,055
Huh, that is weird.

536
00:32:40,693 --> 00:32:43,694
Oh... What is it?

537
00:32:44,930 --> 00:32:49,465
That's a picture
of Knight's Legend.

538
00:32:49,535 --> 00:32:52,668
That's a... a
championship racehorse.

539
00:32:52,737 --> 00:32:54,304
Sam told me all about it.

540
00:32:56,541 --> 00:33:00,043
Well, Sam said
I'd find you here.

541
00:33:00,112 --> 00:33:01,844
You look surprised, Mr. Matlock.

542
00:33:01,914 --> 00:33:04,747
When I first married
Sam, everybody thought

543
00:33:04,816 --> 00:33:07,483
I was a fluffy-headed bimbo
after an older man's money.

544
00:33:07,552 --> 00:33:08,684
They hated me for it.

545
00:33:08,753 --> 00:33:09,753
Yeah.

546
00:33:09,788 --> 00:33:11,554
Now they take me for a smart,

547
00:33:11,623 --> 00:33:13,756
tough-minded woman
capable of running this farm

548
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:17,093
and hate me for
it... except Sam.

549
00:33:17,162 --> 00:33:18,494
As long as Sam loves me,

550
00:33:18,563 --> 00:33:20,263
who cares what
anyone else thinks?

551
00:33:20,332 --> 00:33:22,498
Hmm.

552
00:33:24,736 --> 00:33:26,670
Do you recognize this horse?

553
00:33:27,873 --> 00:33:30,440
Three white stockings
and a sorrel foot.

554
00:33:30,508 --> 00:33:34,310
Looks light old pictures
I've seen of Knight's Legend.

555
00:33:34,379 --> 00:33:35,379
Valuable horse.

556
00:33:35,447 --> 00:33:38,682
That's what I've heard.

557
00:33:42,521 --> 00:33:47,557
Uh, Mr. Purdy, how long
have you been foreman

558
00:33:47,626 --> 00:33:51,862
out at the Taylor
Thoroughbred Horse Farm?

559
00:33:51,930 --> 00:33:53,675
Three, three-and-half years.

560
00:33:53,699 --> 00:33:57,133
Uh-huh. And where did
you work before then?

561
00:33:57,202 --> 00:33:59,214
The Double Daisy
Farm, up in Tennessee.

562
00:33:59,238 --> 00:34:00,270
How many years?

563
00:34:00,338 --> 00:34:01,516
Two or three.

564
00:34:01,540 --> 00:34:03,018
Mm-hmm. And where'd
you work before that?

565
00:34:03,042 --> 00:34:05,153
Well, I don't know. I've
worked many places.

566
00:34:05,177 --> 00:34:07,577
Yeah... Yeah, you have.

567
00:34:07,646 --> 00:34:10,180
In fact, you've held down
more jobs in the past ten years

568
00:34:10,248 --> 00:34:12,393
than most people do in
a lifetime, haven't you?

569
00:34:12,417 --> 00:34:13,650
Objection: relevancy.

570
00:34:13,719 --> 00:34:15,252
It calls for speculation.

571
00:34:15,320 --> 00:34:17,254
Sustained.

572
00:34:17,322 --> 00:34:21,124
Yes, why, why did you
move around so much?

573
00:34:21,193 --> 00:34:22,670
It was just the way things were.

574
00:34:22,694 --> 00:34:26,996
Uh-huh. Mr. Purdy, uh,
you like to do a little drinking

575
00:34:27,065 --> 00:34:28,431
while you're working, don't ya?

576
00:34:28,500 --> 00:34:30,767
Not anymore. I'm
clean and sober.

577
00:34:30,836 --> 00:34:34,003
Well, now, Patricia Taylor
and John Donovan work

578
00:34:34,072 --> 00:34:35,772
with you every day.

579
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:37,407
I don't expect they would agree

580
00:34:37,476 --> 00:34:39,587
that you've quit
drinking, do you? Well, I...

581
00:34:39,611 --> 00:34:42,745
I'm sure that Sandra either
knew it or suspected it.

582
00:34:42,814 --> 00:34:44,793
You had an argument
with her about it,

583
00:34:44,817 --> 00:34:46,094
didn't you? I did not.

584
00:34:46,118 --> 00:34:51,888
Who are these,
these fellas here, um...

585
00:34:51,957 --> 00:34:55,692
Norman Stroud, Eugene
Buford, Tex Rafferty?

586
00:34:55,761 --> 00:34:57,126
They're all foremen.

587
00:34:57,196 --> 00:34:58,561
Top-of-the-line foremen.

588
00:34:58,630 --> 00:35:00,330
Yes. And you knew

589
00:35:00,399 --> 00:35:02,009
that Sandra had
called all of them

590
00:35:02,033 --> 00:35:03,666
and offered your job to them.

591
00:35:03,735 --> 00:35:04,567
No, I did not.

592
00:35:04,636 --> 00:35:06,202
She was gonna fire you.

593
00:35:06,271 --> 00:35:08,037
It was just a matter of time.

594
00:35:08,106 --> 00:35:10,173
And you dared not lose this job

595
00:35:10,242 --> 00:35:13,276
because if you lose
this job, chances are

596
00:35:13,345 --> 00:35:14,465
you'd never get another one.

597
00:35:14,513 --> 00:35:15,878
She wasn't gonna fire me.

598
00:35:15,948 --> 00:35:19,148
You went to her, you pled with
her to give you one more chance.

599
00:35:19,217 --> 00:35:21,818
And when she refused,
you took Tommy's knife

600
00:35:21,887 --> 00:35:23,098
put on your old work clothes...

601
00:35:23,122 --> 00:35:24,432
No. And you killed her.

602
00:35:24,456 --> 00:35:28,224
And who better to frame
than this poor innocent boy.

603
00:35:28,293 --> 00:35:30,660
But you continued to provoke him

604
00:35:30,729 --> 00:35:33,129
till he ran away and made
himself look even more guilty

605
00:35:33,197 --> 00:35:34,442
No!

606
00:35:34,466 --> 00:35:37,600
When she told me
she was gonna fire me,

607
00:35:37,669 --> 00:35:39,302
I was plenty mad all right.

608
00:35:39,371 --> 00:35:42,005
I went down to the
Continental Bar that night

609
00:35:42,074 --> 00:35:43,874
and I started drinking.

610
00:35:43,942 --> 00:35:47,355
And I didn't quit drinking till I
passed out in the middle of the floor.

611
00:35:47,379 --> 00:35:49,112
Ask the bartender.

612
00:35:49,181 --> 00:35:55,051
Ask all the people who had to
step over my carcass all night.

613
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:58,621
I started drinking
again, it's true.

614
00:35:58,690 --> 00:36:01,090
But I didn't kill Sandra.

615
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:12,468
No further questions.

616
00:36:12,538 --> 00:36:14,904
Ms. March, redirect?

617
00:36:14,972 --> 00:36:16,172
No, Your Honor.

618
00:36:16,241 --> 00:36:20,342
This court is in recess
until 10:00 Monday morning.

619
00:36:20,412 --> 00:36:22,178
Is it over now?

620
00:36:22,247 --> 00:36:24,180
Not yet.

621
00:36:32,157 --> 00:36:33,935
Are you sure?

622
00:36:33,959 --> 00:36:37,360
You sure it's not a coincidence?

623
00:36:37,428 --> 00:36:38,361
Huh.

624
00:36:38,429 --> 00:36:39,674
Okay. Well, thank you.

625
00:36:39,698 --> 00:36:40,975
Thank you very much.

626
00:36:40,999 --> 00:36:42,810
Let's go. Where we going?

627
00:36:42,834 --> 00:36:44,812
Out to the Taylor farm.

628
00:36:44,836 --> 00:36:47,048
Does Tyler have something
special going on this weekend?

629
00:36:47,072 --> 00:36:48,138
Not that I know of.

630
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:50,766
Good. I got something
I want him to do.

631
00:37:00,051 --> 00:37:01,951
Hey, Tyler, you
finding anything?

632
00:37:03,922 --> 00:37:05,087
Hell, no!

633
00:37:07,959 --> 00:37:09,658
Keep digging!

634
00:37:14,166 --> 00:37:17,834
Mr. Taylor, you've
raised thoroughbreds

635
00:37:17,903 --> 00:37:20,236
for 45 years.

636
00:37:20,305 --> 00:37:22,906
Now, how do you make
money in your business?

637
00:37:22,975 --> 00:37:25,341
You raise horses
that, uh, win all the time

638
00:37:25,410 --> 00:37:27,644
and make you a lot
of money at the track?

639
00:37:27,713 --> 00:37:29,457
Well, I want the
horses that we raise

640
00:37:29,481 --> 00:37:31,826
to bring home as many
purses as they can, yes.

641
00:37:31,850 --> 00:37:34,583
But I also want the
horses to make me money

642
00:37:34,652 --> 00:37:36,231
after their racing
career's over.

643
00:37:36,255 --> 00:37:37,332
You're talking about stud fees.

644
00:37:37,356 --> 00:37:38,288
Yes, sir.

645
00:37:38,357 --> 00:37:40,790
The real object of the game

646
00:37:40,858 --> 00:37:43,593
is to raise a champion
for whose offspring,

647
00:37:43,662 --> 00:37:45,829
other breeders will
pay handsomely.

648
00:37:45,897 --> 00:37:49,632
Would you tell the court
who, uh, Knight's Legend was.

649
00:37:49,701 --> 00:37:52,636
Ah... that's the best
horse I ever raised.

650
00:37:52,704 --> 00:37:54,771
True champion, inside and out.

651
00:37:54,840 --> 00:37:56,940
Won every race he ever entered

652
00:37:57,009 --> 00:37:59,375
and would have been
worth millions in stud fees.

653
00:37:59,444 --> 00:38:01,244
What happened?

654
00:38:01,312 --> 00:38:02,679
I got greedy.

655
00:38:02,748 --> 00:38:04,413
He was a proven commodity.

656
00:38:04,482 --> 00:38:05,949
There was absolutely no reason

657
00:38:06,018 --> 00:38:08,351
for that horse
ever to race again.

658
00:38:08,419 --> 00:38:10,286
Except that I knew he'd win,

659
00:38:10,355 --> 00:38:12,499
and I wanted the money.

660
00:38:12,523 --> 00:38:15,091
So I entered him in
a big handicap race.

661
00:38:15,160 --> 00:38:17,293
And he shattered a foreleg

662
00:38:17,362 --> 00:38:20,296
about 20 yards
from the finish line.

663
00:38:20,365 --> 00:38:23,967
We took him home, but,
uh, it didn't do any good.

664
00:38:24,036 --> 00:38:26,936
I just had to have
him destroyed.

665
00:38:27,005 --> 00:38:27,937
Who put him down? You?

666
00:38:28,005 --> 00:38:28,938
No, no.

667
00:38:29,007 --> 00:38:30,173
I had my foreman do it.

668
00:38:30,241 --> 00:38:32,441
I-I couldn't even bear to watch.

669
00:38:32,511 --> 00:38:34,743
Your foreman, uh, Clint Purdy?

670
00:38:34,813 --> 00:38:35,912
Oh, no.

671
00:38:35,981 --> 00:38:38,126
Mr. John Donovan was
my foreman at the time.

672
00:38:39,618 --> 00:38:42,118
He took a .38 pistol and
a shovel out into the field,

673
00:38:42,186 --> 00:38:45,721
and he didn't come back
until after he buried him.

674
00:38:45,791 --> 00:38:48,057
Well, thank you very much.

675
00:38:48,126 --> 00:38:49,236
And no further questions.

676
00:38:49,260 --> 00:38:50,193
Your witness.

677
00:38:50,262 --> 00:38:51,894
No questions, Your Honor.

678
00:38:51,963 --> 00:38:53,696
Witness may step down.

679
00:38:53,765 --> 00:38:57,133
Call John Donovan to the stand.

680
00:38:57,202 --> 00:38:59,469
Now, Mr. Donovan,

681
00:38:59,538 --> 00:39:02,271
how long have you worked
out at the Taylor ranch?

682
00:39:02,341 --> 00:39:04,974
Close to 25 years.

683
00:39:05,042 --> 00:39:06,242
And, uh,

684
00:39:06,311 --> 00:39:10,146
you and Mr. Taylor were
very good, very old friends,

685
00:39:10,215 --> 00:39:11,314
weren't you?

686
00:39:11,383 --> 00:39:12,314
Still are.

687
00:39:12,384 --> 00:39:16,552
Uh, at-at-at one point,

688
00:39:16,621 --> 00:39:20,757
he talked with you about,
uh, making you a partner,

689
00:39:20,826 --> 00:39:22,658
didn't he?

690
00:39:22,727 --> 00:39:24,060
We discussed it, yes.

691
00:39:24,129 --> 00:39:25,060
Yeah, yeah.

692
00:39:25,130 --> 00:39:26,895
But, uh, but that didn't,

693
00:39:26,964 --> 00:39:28,931
uh, that didn't work out.

694
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:30,800
No.

695
00:39:32,904 --> 00:39:37,807
And, uh, up until, oh,
three and a half years ago,

696
00:39:37,875 --> 00:39:40,510
you were foreman, but then,

697
00:39:40,579 --> 00:39:42,878
that was taken away from you.

698
00:39:42,947 --> 00:39:46,416
When Sandra took over the
farm, she did some reorganizing,

699
00:39:46,484 --> 00:39:48,651
gave my job to Clint Purdy.

700
00:39:48,719 --> 00:39:49,730
Which was fine with me.

701
00:39:50,755 --> 00:39:52,021
It's a young man's job, anyway.

702
00:39:52,090 --> 00:39:56,492
You ever get the feeling
you're being shoved aside?

703
00:39:56,561 --> 00:39:58,661
No.

704
00:40:00,765 --> 00:40:03,999
Oh. Uh, have you ever,

705
00:40:04,068 --> 00:40:05,635
have you ever seen this picture?

706
00:40:06,738 --> 00:40:08,438
No.

707
00:40:08,507 --> 00:40:10,239
You know who this horse is?

708
00:40:10,308 --> 00:40:11,974
No.

709
00:40:14,078 --> 00:40:17,213
Don't you think he looks a
little bit like Knight's Legend?

710
00:40:17,282 --> 00:40:19,115
Yeah, I guess.

711
00:40:19,184 --> 00:40:20,116
Yeah.

712
00:40:20,185 --> 00:40:22,318
I do. I do.

713
00:40:22,387 --> 00:40:27,990
I, um... I had that
picture blown up.

714
00:40:28,059 --> 00:40:31,394
Look at that. Look at that.

715
00:40:31,462 --> 00:40:32,961
That nice?

716
00:40:33,031 --> 00:40:34,263
I had it blown up.

717
00:40:34,332 --> 00:40:35,565
And, uh, look here.

718
00:40:35,633 --> 00:40:36,913
See, right under the tote board,

719
00:40:36,968 --> 00:40:40,503
says, "J-E-F-F"
and looks like an "E."

720
00:40:40,572 --> 00:40:44,874
So I took a chance and
called Jefferson Downs.

721
00:40:44,943 --> 00:40:46,587
That's a little track
outside of Tallahassee.

722
00:40:46,611 --> 00:40:47,731
You ever been over there?

723
00:40:47,779 --> 00:40:49,011
Many times. Yeah.

724
00:40:49,080 --> 00:40:51,981
And I was just curious when
this race might have been run.

725
00:40:52,050 --> 00:40:54,584
And so I asked
them if they could tell

726
00:40:54,653 --> 00:40:57,119
by the odds up over
the tote board there

727
00:40:57,188 --> 00:40:59,166
when it was run and
if they had a record.

728
00:40:59,190 --> 00:41:00,489
And you know, they did.

729
00:41:00,559 --> 00:41:03,259
They had a record
of it in their computer.

730
00:41:03,327 --> 00:41:07,396
And this race was run
March 19 of this year...

731
00:41:07,465 --> 00:41:08,397
Three months ago.

732
00:41:08,466 --> 00:41:10,499
Guess it can't be a picture

733
00:41:10,569 --> 00:41:12,379
of Knight's Legend then, can it?

734
00:41:12,403 --> 00:41:14,169
No, no.

735
00:41:14,239 --> 00:41:15,170
No.

736
00:41:15,240 --> 00:41:16,805
It could be a picture

737
00:41:16,874 --> 00:41:19,542
of Knight's Legend's
colt though, couldn't it?

738
00:41:19,611 --> 00:41:22,111
Well, that's impossible.

739
00:41:22,179 --> 00:41:23,646
You heard Mr. Taylor.

740
00:41:23,715 --> 00:41:24,947
Knight's Legend was destroyed

741
00:41:25,016 --> 00:41:27,349
before he could be
used for breeding.

742
00:41:27,419 --> 00:41:30,052
He was supposed to be.

743
00:41:30,121 --> 00:41:32,688
But was he, Mr. Donovan?

744
00:41:32,757 --> 00:41:34,256
Yes. I buried him myself.

745
00:41:34,325 --> 00:41:35,691
Where?

746
00:41:35,760 --> 00:41:38,294
The edge of the south
pasture, where it's fenced off.

747
00:41:38,363 --> 00:41:41,497
That whole area was
dug up this weekend.

748
00:41:41,565 --> 00:41:42,765
There's nothing buried there.

749
00:41:45,537 --> 00:41:48,071
You never put him down, did you?

750
00:41:48,139 --> 00:41:50,106
Yes, I did.

751
00:41:52,209 --> 00:41:55,111
You felt you had
nothing to lose.

752
00:41:55,179 --> 00:41:57,713
You were losing everything
at the farm anyway.

753
00:41:57,782 --> 00:42:00,416
And you know,

754
00:42:00,485 --> 00:42:03,653
if it had turned
out differently,

755
00:42:03,722 --> 00:42:06,222
everybody would've
been so grateful.

756
00:42:07,325 --> 00:42:10,860
You hauled that horse off.

757
00:42:10,929 --> 00:42:13,262
And with the tricks
and knowledge

758
00:42:13,331 --> 00:42:17,066
you've learned over the years,
you nursed him back to health,

759
00:42:17,135 --> 00:42:18,301
didn't you?

760
00:42:18,369 --> 00:42:19,646
No, you don't know
what you're saying.

761
00:42:19,670 --> 00:42:20,670
That's impossible.

762
00:42:22,707 --> 00:42:25,041
You don't call him
Knight's Legend, no.

763
00:42:25,110 --> 00:42:27,577
And you had to
forge a lot of papers,

764
00:42:27,645 --> 00:42:29,745
and you had to do
something about the tattoo

765
00:42:29,814 --> 00:42:32,781
that all thoroughbreds
have under their upper lip.

766
00:42:32,851 --> 00:42:37,186
But that horse
is alive and well.

767
00:42:37,255 --> 00:42:38,354
Isn't he?

768
00:42:38,423 --> 00:42:40,201
I'm telling you,
that's impossible.

769
00:42:40,225 --> 00:42:44,694
Mr. Donovan, you
should never have thrown

770
00:42:44,763 --> 00:42:47,630
your credit card receipts on
the floorboard of your truck.

771
00:42:47,699 --> 00:42:52,234
Too easy for my
man Tyler to find.

772
00:42:52,303 --> 00:42:54,849
I know why you've been
buying so much gasoline

773
00:42:54,873 --> 00:42:56,918
over at Piedmont, Alabama.

774
00:42:56,942 --> 00:43:00,576
Because you've
been boarding a horse

775
00:43:00,645 --> 00:43:04,446
at a little stable
outside of town.

776
00:43:06,517 --> 00:43:07,517
That horse.

777
00:43:11,456 --> 00:43:14,190
That's Knight's Legend.

778
00:43:18,430 --> 00:43:19,574
This court will come to order!

779
00:43:19,598 --> 00:43:21,764
Your Honor, I object!

780
00:43:21,833 --> 00:43:22,765
Order!

781
00:43:22,833 --> 00:43:24,634
Order in the court!

782
00:43:24,702 --> 00:43:27,403
Now, please be seated.

783
00:43:27,472 --> 00:43:29,483
Mr. Matlock, how
long do you intend

784
00:43:29,507 --> 00:43:31,452
to have this animal
in my courtroom?

785
00:43:31,476 --> 00:43:34,610
Your Honor, this
is not a Bengal tiger

786
00:43:34,679 --> 00:43:36,345
or a python snake.

787
00:43:36,414 --> 00:43:38,914
This is just a brown
horse who likes people.

788
00:43:38,983 --> 00:43:40,182
See?

789
00:43:40,251 --> 00:43:42,184
Nice horsey.

790
00:43:42,253 --> 00:43:43,452
A few moments, Your Honor.

791
00:43:43,521 --> 00:43:45,254
I'll hold you to that.

792
00:43:45,323 --> 00:43:46,588
Yes, sir.

793
00:43:50,128 --> 00:43:54,063
Mr. Donovan, perhaps you'd
like to change your testimony.

794
00:43:56,868 --> 00:43:59,568
That is Knight's
Legend, isn't it?

795
00:43:59,638 --> 00:44:01,437
Yes.

796
00:44:03,541 --> 00:44:08,010
It must have taken
every penny you had

797
00:44:08,079 --> 00:44:10,713
to board that
horse all this time.

798
00:44:10,782 --> 00:44:13,282
That's why you're still
working at the ranch.

799
00:44:13,351 --> 00:44:15,584
You couldn't make
much on stud fees,

800
00:44:15,653 --> 00:44:17,854
because you had to keep
his existence a secret.

801
00:44:17,922 --> 00:44:21,223
All you could do is wait

802
00:44:21,292 --> 00:44:25,895
for an offspring to
race and hopefully win.

803
00:44:28,733 --> 00:44:31,233
And this is a photograph

804
00:44:31,302 --> 00:44:35,138
of Knight's Legend's
offspring, isn't it?

805
00:44:37,208 --> 00:44:38,208
Yes.

806
00:44:40,244 --> 00:44:42,164
You know where
I got this picture?

807
00:44:44,182 --> 00:44:47,349
From Sandra Taylor's briefcase.

808
00:44:47,418 --> 00:44:49,396
I don't know where she
got it... Doesn't matter.

809
00:44:49,420 --> 00:44:52,855
But I am sure the instant
she saw this photograph,

810
00:44:52,924 --> 00:44:56,092
she saw the resemblance
to Knight's Legend.

811
00:44:56,161 --> 00:44:58,560
She showed it
to you, didn't she?

812
00:44:58,630 --> 00:44:59,862
Why would she do that?

813
00:44:59,931 --> 00:45:00,863
I don't know.

814
00:45:00,932 --> 00:45:03,432
Maybe to see what you thought.

815
00:45:03,501 --> 00:45:08,537
But... when she
showed it to you,

816
00:45:08,606 --> 00:45:11,507
you knew it was
only a matter of time

817
00:45:11,575 --> 00:45:13,075
before she put it all together.

818
00:45:13,144 --> 00:45:17,412
And then, it would
truly all be over.

819
00:45:17,482 --> 00:45:19,949
So that night,

820
00:45:20,018 --> 00:45:22,618
when Tommy left the bunkhouse,

821
00:45:22,686 --> 00:45:27,256
you put on your work
gloves, took Tommy's knife,

822
00:45:27,325 --> 00:45:30,793
went up to Sandra's
office and killed her.

823
00:45:30,862 --> 00:45:34,263
And then you started
looking for this picture.

824
00:45:34,332 --> 00:45:35,998
You looked in her briefcase,

825
00:45:36,067 --> 00:45:37,945
throwing stuff here and
there out of her briefcase.

826
00:45:37,969 --> 00:45:39,101
In the wastebasket,

827
00:45:39,170 --> 00:45:40,914
throwing stuff in and
out of the briefcase.

828
00:45:40,938 --> 00:45:43,072
Tommy's coming all the time!

829
00:45:43,141 --> 00:45:47,342
And you finally, you put
stuff back in the briefcase.

830
00:45:47,411 --> 00:45:50,146
New stuff, old stuff,
papers out of the trash can.

831
00:45:50,214 --> 00:45:52,547
You never found the picture
because Tommy was coming.

832
00:45:52,617 --> 00:45:56,486
Tommy was coming.
Tommy was coming.

833
00:46:01,159 --> 00:46:05,594
And you wanted
Tommy... to take the blame,

834
00:46:05,663 --> 00:46:07,196
didn't you?

835
00:46:57,115 --> 00:46:58,147
Isn't he pretty?

836
00:47:01,819 --> 00:47:03,097
Hey.

837
00:47:03,121 --> 00:47:04,587
Did he bite you?

838
00:47:04,656 --> 00:47:06,722
No.

839
00:47:06,790 --> 00:47:07,956
He remembered me.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
